  "self_review": [
    "Reused the existing bounded independent-thread pattern instead of Tokio spawn_blocking: an uninterruptible network FS call must not keep the async Runtime alive. Work takes a verified target and files only, never SQLite.",
    "Close removes the UI entry and sets stop; worker owns its permit through result destruction and actual return. Channels hold four actual workers at a deterministic boundary; no new work is accepted just because UI jobs were removed.",
    "Late success is discarded, exact accepted UUID retries reuse work, close-before-start and late retries fail within the lease. Cache/idle/closed-lease saturation are bounded; accepted retries and existing cancellation still work when the closed lease soft cap is full.",
    "Core derives Current User. Every poll/page re-resolves the saved original reference under the database mutex, then compares the exact root scope. Descendants inherit that root and only a signed already-verified child can start; closing a parent viewer is not a new grant.",
    "Core resolve failure cancels the read; cleanup remains User-only, idempotent and possible after source deletion. No Runtime stop, domain write, schema or model context is introduced.",
    "Source/parse failures expose fixed codes only. Web has explicit read-view/page/close field allowlists, with original long fragment preserved; Native/Web allowlist tests are transport seams rather than live HTTP/IPC proof.",
    "Review after the first successful binary found Utc::now fallback could shift timestamps on a new read of logs missing time. Final start captures durable Core run creation time; the source owner asserts that exact fallback, and final compile02 and both owners passed.",
    "Idle expiry is lazy on access, not a precise timer. Whole parsed projections remain resident memory, so 16 cache entries do not prove a global byte bound. Original viewer, actual Core/Host/network/GUI, broad performance and full I04 Runtime/format cases remain required."
  ],
